spec fp01-later-commits-ack-behind-held-straggler: 2 sessions, 2 permutations
# FP01. s0 writes s and reserves its commit instant without publishing it (the commit
# hold). s1 then commits 2048 single-node transactions from 8 goroutines through autocommit Cypher: every one
# returns while s0 is held (no step <waiting ...>), and none is visible to a sessionless
# reader, because a commit above an in-flight one is invisible until it publishes (F11).
# When s0 publishes, the frontier catches up in one step: all of them become visible
# together. The control interleaving runs the fan before the hold.

starting permutation: s0w s0a s1fan s1lag s1fr s0p s1seen
step s0w: lpg: SetNodeProperty(s, v, 1)
step s0a: lpg: Graph.AllocateCommitTS (instant reserved, not published)
step s1fan: <8 goroutines x 256 autocommit CREATE (:W)>
step s1lag: <sessionless> MATCH (n:W) RETURN count(n) AS visible
visible
-------
0      
(1 row)
step s1fr: <MVCCStats: in_flight_commits, sessions_waiting>
in_flight_commits|sessions_waiting
-----------------+----------------
2049             |0               
(1 row)
step s0p: lpg: Session.EndVersionedTx
step s1seen: <sessionless> MATCH (n:W) RETURN count(n) AS visible
visible
-------
2048   
(1 row)
final ffr: <MVCCStats: in_flight_commits, sessions_waiting>
in_flight_commits|sessions_waiting
-----------------+----------------
0                |0               
(1 row)
final final: MATCH (n:S {name:'s'}) RETURN n.v AS v
v
-
1
(1 row)

